From 3166f927497e4367e076becffd5061318604531a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reza Jelveh <agent@jelveh.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mock): complete the HAMi bind in Allocate

HAMi's scheduler marks a pod hami.io/bind-phase=allocating and takes the
node lock hami.io/mutex.lock in Bind. The real device plugins finish that
at the end of Allocate: they mark the pod success and release the lock.
The mock plugin's Allocate returned empty responses only, so every mocked
pod stayed "allocating" forever and the next pod on the node waited for
the lock to expire (5 minutes by default) before it could be bound.

Allocate now resolves the pod like HAMi's util.GetPendingPod (the pod the
node lock names, else a Pending allocating pod bound to this node),
patches hami.io/bind-phase=success (conditional on the pod uid) and
releases the lock (conditional on the node resourceVersion). kubelet
calls Allocate once per mocked resource a container requests, so the
completion is idempotent; a failure is logged and never fails Allocate.

The plugin needs pods get/list/patch for this; k8s-mock-rbac.yaml grants
it. Tests use the fake clientset.

Signed-off-by: Reza Jelveh <agent@jelveh.me>
